# Never upload server-build artifacts as public static assets.
# Astro copies public/ into dist/, so this file ships at the root of the
# assets directory, where wrangler reads it. On a clean static build these
# files don't exist; if a deploy adapter (e.g. @astrojs/cloudflare, which
# Cloudflare's Astro framework preset likes to inject) sneaks into the
# build, wrangler would otherwise hard-error with "Uploading a Pages
# _worker.js directory as an asset". Every page is prerendered
# (see astro.config.mjs), so excluding the worker loses nothing.
_worker.js
_routes.json
